# DTF tier manifest: replicated-and-chunked-uploads
# (artifact-keeper#4403/#1846 chunked completion runs the incus/debian native
# finalize; #4404/#3916 no local spool for uploads into object storage)
# Profile-set: s3 (MinIO) / two replicas on one database and one /data volume.
#   storage.s3                 MinIO, backend on STORAGE_BACKEND=s3
#   topology.two-replica       backend-b, reached at 127.0.0.1:8081 inside
#                              backend's network namespace
#   topology.two-replica-s3    backend-b on the same MinIO (new, additive)
#
# Test PR #415 (tests/platform/test-chunked-upload-multi-replica.sh) owns the
# generic cross-replica chunked upload (#3918) and staged-chunk cleanup
# (#3922); this tier keeps one generic cross-replica upload only as a CONTROL
# and asserts what #415 does not:
#   (FIX #4403/#1846) a chunked upload into an incus repository (session and
#        chunk 0 on A, chunk 1 and completion on B) is named after its
#        product/version and carries metadata.yaml's os/release in
#        artifact_metadata and images.json; into a debian repository it is
#        catalogued as its control file's package and indexed with Depends and
#        Description; a .deb whose control disagrees with its file name is
#        refused with 400.
#   (FIX #4404) a multipart POST, and (FIX #3916) a raw PUT, of 8 MiB at
#        1 MiB/s into the MinIO-backed repository: no new file appears on the
#        replicas' /data volume while it streams (a watcher container lists
#        it every 0.25 s), a generic_upload_staging row exists during the
#        upload, and neither rows nor generic-upload-staging/ objects remain.
#   (CONTROL) every upload completes and downloads byte-identical on both
#        images.
# RED: ak-backend:1.10.0. GREEN: 1.11.0 and later.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle polls Postgres and the API while the
# slow uploads stream.
PROFILES="storage.s3 topology.two-replica topology.two-replica-s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
